1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,981
Hematopoietic stem cell transplantation
can cure some cancers and blood diseases,

2
00:00:05,981 --> 00:00:08,636
but the chemotherapy and antibiotics given

3
00:00:08,636 --> 00:00:11,418
beforehand badly damage the gut
microbiome.

4
00:00:11,418 --> 00:00:16,792
Patients who lose microbial diversity also
have higher transplant-related mortality.

5
00:00:16,792 --> 00:00:20,438
Autologous fecal microbiota
transplantation, or auto-FMT,

6
00:00:20,438 --> 00:00:25,363
banks the patient's own stool microbes and
returns them after the transplant,

7
00:00:25,363 --> 00:00:27,474
hoping to restore the microbiome.

8
00:00:28,433 --> 00:00:32,184
In this unit, we use sequencing data to
answer three questions.

9
00:00:32,184 --> 00:00:35,638
How does the gut microbiome change during
transplantation?

10
00:00:35,638 --> 00:00:40,104
Do patients who receive auto-FMT change
differently from the control group?

11
00:00:40,104 --> 00:00:43,438
And which bacteria rise and fall with
transplant timing?

12
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,588
The data come from a clinical trial used
in the official QIIME 2 tutorial,

13
00:00:49,588 --> 00:00:53,444
with patients randomly assigned to
auto-FMT or control.

14
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:56,879
Upstream are raw sequencing files for 41
samples;

15
00:00:56,879 --> 00:01:00,174
downstream is a public table of 12,546
samples.

16
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:05,352
This kind of analysis usually means
knowing Linux, Slurm,

17
00:01:05,352 --> 00:01:06,906
and QIIME 2 commands.

18
00:01:06,906 --> 00:01:11,864
Unit 05 shows another way: open an AI
Agent on the NCHC HPC system,

19
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:16,527
and run the whole analysis through
plain-language conversation.

20
00:01:17,467 --> 00:01:22,192
There are four steps: download the data,
confirm the account and queue,

21
00:01:22,192 --> 00:01:26,318
submit the job, and finally ask the AI for
an analysis report.

22
00:01:27,267 --> 00:01:32,441
Step one: paste the download link and ask
the AI to download and extract it.

23
00:01:32,441 --> 00:01:35,844
The data and the analysis script are now
in place.

24
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:39,404
Step two: not sure which project account

25
00:01:39,404 --> 00:01:41,161
or queue to use? Just ask.

26
00:01:41,161 --> 00:01:46,314
The AI checks the Slurm settings itself,
confirms that MST109178 is available,

27
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:50,873
and explains that the course queue,
ngscourse8g, is enough this time,

28
00:01:50,873 --> 00:01:55,499
because the most demanding step,
denoising, has already been computed.

29
00:01:56,433 --> 00:02:00,610
Step three: say "Go ahead and submit it,"
and the job is on its way.

30
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:03,682
Then ask for a progress report every five
minutes,

31
00:02:03,682 --> 00:02:06,692
so you don't have to watch the commands
yourself.

32
00:02:06,692 --> 00:02:10,010
Eighteen minutes later, the job finishes
successfully.

33
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:16,488
The run leaves a pile of qza and qzv files
that are hard to read at a glance.

34
00:02:16,488 --> 00:02:21,938
Step four: ask the AI for a report with
one section and figure per analysis,

35
00:02:21,938 --> 00:02:23,659
ending with conclusions.

36
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:28,821
Seventeen minutes later, it delivers a
nine-page PDF with eight figures.

37
00:02:29,767 --> 00:02:30,994
Now the report.

38
00:02:30,994 --> 00:02:36,965
First, filtering: starting from 12,546
samples, filtering by trial group,

39
00:02:36,965 --> 00:02:43,509
transplant time window, and sequencing
depth leaves 24 patients and 356 samples,

40
00:02:43,509 --> 00:02:45,963
nearly 15 samples per patient.

41
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,894
In taxonomic composition,

42
00:02:48,894 --> 00:02:54,876
Enterococcaceae averages under 1% before
transplant and rises to 22% after.

43
00:02:54,876 --> 00:03:00,540
Of the 225 post-transplant samples, 48 are
more than half Enterococcus,

44
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:05,405
the single-taxon domination often seen
after transplantation.

45
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:09,701
Microbial richness drops sharply after
transplant,

46
00:03:09,701 --> 00:03:13,568
and the before-and-after difference is
highly significant.

47
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,702
But with all time points pooled,

48
00:03:15,702 --> 00:03:20,169
the auto-FMT and control groups show no
difference: p equals 0.256.

49
00:03:21,133 --> 00:03:24,156
The beta diversity ordination tells the
same story:

50
00:03:24,156 --> 00:03:28,601
pre-transplant samples cluster together,
while during and after transplant,

51
00:03:28,601 --> 00:03:31,565
the community clearly shifts away and
spreads out.

52
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:37,367
Each patient was sampled many times, so we
need a longitudinal model.

53
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:42,656
A linear mixed-effects model shows
richness in the control group falling by

54
00:03:42,656 --> 00:03:47,311
about 0.86 per day, while the auto-FMT
group declines more slowly:

55
00:03:47,311 --> 00:03:50,838
a slope difference of 0.56, with p equal
to 0.016.

56
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:57,102
A random forest uses taxon proportions to
predict the week after transplant,

57
00:03:57,102 --> 00:03:58,985
with an R-squared of 0.319.

58
00:03:58,985 --> 00:04:02,962
The top features are Enterococcaceae and
Lachnospiraceae.

59
00:04:02,962 --> 00:04:06,380
Note that it predicts time, not treatment
effect.

60
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:09,202
Back to our three questions.

61
00:04:09,202 --> 00:04:12,872
Transplantation sharply reduces gut
microbial richness,

62
00:04:12,872 --> 00:04:14,741
and Enterococcus takes over.

63
00:04:14,741 --> 00:04:19,880
Pooling all samples, the two groups look
the same; with a longitudinal model,

64
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:22,550
the auto-FMT group declines more slowly.

65
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:27,155
And the bacteria that rise and fall with
transplant timing are mainly

66
00:04:27,155 --> 00:04:29,557
Enterococcaceae and Lachnospiraceae.

67
00:04:29,557 --> 00:04:33,428
But with only 24 patients, this is a lead
worth following,

68
00:04:33,428 --> 00:04:35,764
not proof that the treatment works.

69
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,502
The analysis is done and the report is
ready, but

70
00:04:39,502 --> 00:04:42,190
a report is not yet a paper. In the next
unit,

71
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:46,813
we take these results and work with AI to
write an English paper with citations.

